.TH FLEXFETCH 1 "July 2026" "flexfetch 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flexfetch \- fast, flexible system information tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flexfetch
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flexfetch
displays system information with customizable themes and output formats.
It collects data about the operating system, hardware, and environment,
then renders it through configurable templates.
.PP
Modules can be selected individually, via presets, or via module groups.
Output can be piped, exported to SVG/HTML/PNG, or displayed with themed
formatting.
.PP
A live dashboard (\fB--live\fR), an interactive config wizard
(\fB--wizard\fR), remote SSH fetching (\fB--ssh\fR), and shell
completions generation are also included.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to configuration file.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-modules " " \fIMODULES\fR
Colon-separated list of modules to display.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-template " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to custom Tera template file.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: \fBtext\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, \fBsvg\fR, \fBhtml\fR, \fBpng\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " " \fINAME\fR
Apply a color theme.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output.
.TP
.B \-\-gen-config
Generate default configuration file at ~/.config/flexfetch/config.toml.
.TP
.B \-\-list-modules
List all available modules.
.TP
.B \-\-list-presets
List all available presets (built-in and user-defined).
.TP
.BR \-\-benchmark " " [ N ]
Run a performance benchmark of each module. With an optional iteration count
\fIN\fR, run the full pipeline N times and report min/avg timings.
.TP
.B \-\-smart
Add \fI\$PWD\fR context modules: git branch/status, project type, container/venv/SSH.
.TP
.B \-\-health
Add the system health module (score 0\-100 from disk/swap/load/battery).
.TP
.B \-\-prompt
Print a single\-line, ANSI\-free prompt string (OS | CPU | RAM).
.TP
.B \-\-motd
Print a plain\-text banner with ANSI colors stripped (for MOTD/startup).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " " \fIHOST\fR ...
Fetch system info from remote host(s) over SSH (repeatable, run in parallel).
Falls back to scp'ing the current binary when the remote lacks flexfetch.
.TP
.B \-\-wizard
Interactive config wizard: pick modules, theme, and layout, then write
~/.config/flexfetch/config.toml. Requires the \fBlive\fR feature.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Refresh output every N seconds (default 2, see --watch-interval).
Hot\-reloads the config file when it changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-watch-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Seconds between watch refreshes (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-live
Real\-time dashboard: CPU/memory gauges with sparklines, top processes,
and network rates. Requires a terminal. Requires the \fBlive\fR feature.
.TP
.B \-\-smart
Add \fI\$PWD\fR context modules: git branch/status, project type,
container/venv/SSH session.
.TP
.BR completions " " \fISHELL\fR
Print shell completions for \fIbash\fR, \fIzsh\fR, \fIfish\fR, etc.
Requires the \fBcompletions\fR feature (default on).
.PP
Example: \fBflexfetch completions bash\fR
.TP
.B \-\-pipe
Force pipe mode (no colors, no boxes).
.TP
.B \-\-minimal
Show minimal set: os, kernel, uptime.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Show all default modules.
.TP
.B \-\-dev
Show developer set: os, cpu, memory, disk, shell, terminal.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset " " \fINAME\fR
Use a named preset. Built-in: default, minimal, full, dev, server, laptop.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Export output to file (svg, html, png).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output file path (used with --export).
.TP
.B \-\-no-gradient
Disable gradient title rendering.
.TP
.B \-\-no-progress
Disable progress bar rendering.
.TP
.BI \-\-box-style " " \fISTYLE\fR
Box rendering style: rounded, sharp, double, heavy.
.TP
.B \-\-pixel-logo
Enable pixel art logo.
.TP
.BI \-\-palette-style " " \fISTYLE\fR
Color palette style: gradient, solid, ansi.
.TP
.BI \-\-frame " " \fISTYLE\fR
Frame style: none, single, double, rounded.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from ~/.config/flexfetch/config.toml.
Use \fBflexfetch --gen-config\fR to create a default configuration.
.PP
Presets are stored in ~/.config/flexfetch/presets/ as .toml files.
.PP
Feature\-gated builds: \fB--no-default-features\fR drops Lua, the live
dashboard, image logos, the Tera template engine, and Rayon for a
~1.5 MB minimal binary (plain \fB\|\|\-\-\|\|\fR tree connectors instead
of templates). See the mdBook docs at
\fBhttps://github.com/mahesh-diwan/flexfetch\fR for the feature matrix.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display default modules:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch
.RE
.PP
Show only CPU and memory:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch -m cpu:memory
.RE
.PP
Export to SVG:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --export svg -o system.svg
.RE
.PP
Use server preset:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --preset server
.RE
.PP
Pipe-friendly output:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --pipe | head -20
.RE
.PP
Shell prompt string:
.PP
.RS 4
PS1="$(flexfetch --prompt) $ "
.RE
.PP
System health score:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --health
.RE
.PP
Remote hosts over SSH (repeatable; each host runs its own default modules):
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --ssh server1 --ssh server2
.RE
.PP
Configure interactively:
.PP
.RS 4
flexfetch --wizard
.RE
